  "notes": {
    "receipt": "The signed receipt v2 payload from section 5 of the receipt spec (https://github.com/babyblueviper1/x402/blob/0e492d6730bef14b9c722428386c114f3475a914/specs/extensions/extension-offer-and-receipt.md). receiptHash is 0x + sha256 of its canonical JSON, the same bytes the private-opening statement's receipt_sha256 covers. The seller's receipt signature is out of scope here, as in the spec's own vectors.",
    "commitment": "authorizationCommitment = 0x + sha256(\"x402-receipt-authorization/0\" 0x00 \"eip3009\" 0x00 asset(20) authorizer(20) nonce(32) salt(32)). authorizer is the receipt's signed payer, never a value supplied with the salt (section 5.6.4 step 1).",
    "counting": "Section 5.6.5: an unopened commitment is unique per receipt, not per payment, so a deduplicated or Sybil-resistant count counts opened commitments only.",
    "why": "A consumer that checks the settlement and skips the opening would credit this receipt with any settlement of the same payer and nonce, which is the link the commitment exists to prove."
  }
